From: pookee <13053375+pookee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:52:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Run inside a host app such as PadHub

- The NSO bridge takes the controllers back each time it starts,
  catching up with controllers that came and went while a host's menu
  had them, without unplugging the ports of those still there. It
  reports the HOME button to the host.
- The overlay puts the host's items (Back to PadHub) at the top of its
  menus.
- dev-config.plist, the bundled disc path and the home emblem come from
  MeleePad's own bundle, so they are found in its framework inside a
  host app.
- stopGame ends the game as Exit to Home does, for a host that starts
  another game.

The standalone app behaves as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
